{
 "assembly_notes": "Hand-operated sheet-metal bending brake. The grounded `frame` part is the bed: a plate with a bending edge rail along +x at y=0, forked hinge ears for both moving members, a rear apron and the adjuster posts behind it. The `clamp_beam` part hinges REVOLUTE about +x at the back of the bed and lifts its nose off the bed, and the `bending_leaf` part hinges REVOLUTE about +x one clearance in front of the bending edge and folds up through a travel that stops just short of the bend line, so it never reaches back under the clamp nose. Each clamp station carries a `handle_{i}` lever on the clamp beam and an `adjuster_{i}` screw on a PRISMATIC slide behind the bed. frame_form varies the ground end: a bare bed, a bench-top pad with bolt lugs, or a welded floor stand with splayed legs; the bed height it sets carries through to both hinge lines and every station. clamp_form varies the clamp face: one continuous bar, bolted segments, removable fingers, or screw-down clamps. leaf_form varies the leaf: one plain plate with a lift bar, or stiffened segments with ribs between them. accessory adds a PRISMATIC bend-stop fence behind the bed or a long centre lever on its own REVOLUTE. brake_width_m, bed_depth_m and leaf_length_m are the honest continuous parameters; clamp_station_count and leaf_rib_count are the multiplicities; palette is neither.",
